# RenderPhase state-shard constants, for consumers building layers through `CustomLayers.create`.
#
# These are `protected static` on `RenderPhase`. SpellEngine's own `CustomLayers` reaches them legally
# (it extends RenderLayer extends RenderPhase), but a *consumer* class that merely passes them as
# arguments -- e.g. Paladins' `BarrierEntityRenderer$Config` -- does not, and the JVM throws
# IllegalAccessError when that class initializes.
#
# It compiles, and runs on Fabric, only because Fabric API's `fabric-transitive-access-wideners-v1`
# module widens all of them. Loom applies that transitive AW to the compile-time jar on BOTH platforms,
# and on Fabric the module is present at runtime so the widening also holds in production. The 1.20.1
# Forge build ships no Forgified Fabric API, so nothing widens them there and the access is real.
# Hence they must be widened here: SpellEngine's AW is converted to a Forge AT by Loom
# (`forge/build.gradle` -> `remapJar { atAccessWideners }`), which patches the game for every consumer,
# so no content mod needs an AT of its own.
#
# Exactly the members the ecosystem uses -- keep this list minimal, and extend it when a consumer
# needs another shard rather than widening the class wholesale.
accessible    field    net/minecraft/client/render/RenderPhase    TRANSLUCENT_TRANSPARENCY    Lnet/minecraft/client/render/RenderPhase$Transparency;
